<title>FRANCE: EU revises Swiss, Liechtenstein grain refunds.</title>
<headline>EU revises Swiss, Liechtenstein grain refunds.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has again raised its standing export refund for soft wheat exports to Switzerland and Liechtenstein but cut refunds in the same bracket for barley and rye, grain trade sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committee which met in Brussels on Thursday set new refunds of 8.0 Ecus per tonne for soft wheat, 21.0 Ecus for rye and 18.0 Ecus for barley, they said.</p>
<p>The EU had previously on January 30 set the refunds at 5.0 Ecus for soft wheat, 22.0 Ecus for rye and 18.5 Ecus for barley.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
